building research skills

00:44:06.900 --> 00:44:09.420
and then doing research during the summer.

00:44:09.420 --> 00:44:12.500
So you would build research
skills in the spring,

00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:15.490
and then in like an afterschool session.

00:44:15.490 --> 00:44:16.680
And then you would build your...

00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:20.096
You would like apply this to actually...

00:44:20.096 --> 00:44:20.929
We would mail you a bunch of stuff,

00:44:20.929 --> 00:44:24.150
and you could do potential
like microbiology experiments,

00:44:24.150 --> 00:44:26.336
or even coding style of experiments,

00:44:26.336 --> 00:44:29.070
in the summer under
mentorship of scientists

00:44:29.070 --> 00:44:31.580
in a program called Lab Jumpstart.

00:44:31.580 --> 00:44:34.480
And you also get a stipend,

00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:35.930
so that you don't have to choose

00:44:35.930 --> 00:44:39.040
between like if working during
the summer is your stick.

00:44:39.040 --> 00:44:41.130
I know I always worked during the summer.

00:44:41.130 --> 00:44:44.840
I would ask my parents
if I could like go to...

00:44:44.840 --> 00:44:48.040
like Columbia had a microbiology program

00:44:48.040 --> 00:44:49.070
for high school students.

00:44:49.070 --> 00:44:50.960
And I really wanted to go to that.

00:44:50.960 --> 00:44:53.110
And my parents were like,
no, you have to work.

00:44:53.110 --> 00:44:56.910
And the Columbia program had
tuition associated with it.

00:44:56.910 --> 00:44:58.420
And my parents were like, no way.

00:44:58.420 --> 00:45:02.070
So we don't want to ever
put any kid in that position

00:45:02.070 --> 00:45:05.650
where you want to do a program like this,

00:45:05.650 --> 00:45:07.453
but you need to also work.

00:45:07.453 --> 00:45:11.670
Maybe that's me like pushing
my own experiences on people.

00:45:11.670 --> 00:45:15.390
But so yeah, we offer a really
nice generous stipend for it.

00:45:15.390 --> 00:45:20.390
So I definitely encourage you to do that.

