00:46:13.070 --> 00:46:15.110
I got a 4.0 one semester.

00:46:15.110 --> 00:46:16.320
And there was just like

00:46:16.320 --> 00:46:18.013
that seems like a low number.

00:46:20.330 --> 00:46:23.530
So it's I had to do,

00:46:23.530 --> 00:46:25.920
I had to navigate this
whole place by myself.

00:46:25.920 --> 00:46:29.009
And that's exactly why
we built the programs

00:46:29.009 --> 00:46:30.230
that we built.

00:46:30.230 --> 00:46:32.320
It's for you to not have to go

00:46:32.320 --> 00:46:34.870
through that BS that I had to go through

00:46:34.870 --> 00:46:37.490
of like sinking or swimming.

00:46:37.490 --> 00:46:38.890
Like, that's not okay.

00:46:38.890 --> 00:46:40.510
People should be supporting each other.

00:46:40.510 --> 00:46:42.630
And these programs are
designed specifically

00:46:42.630 --> 00:46:44.300
to make sure that even

00:46:44.300 --> 00:46:45.950
if you feel not confident about yourself,

00:46:45.950 --> 00:46:47.630
and none of us feel
confident about ourselves,

00:46:47.630 --> 00:46:50.800
like 100% of the time,
so that's totally normal.

00:46:50.800 --> 00:46:52.820
But like, we want to build you up.

00:46:52.820 --> 00:46:56.390
I believe in building people,
who then build good science,

00:46:56.390 --> 00:46:58.380
but if you don't have good people,

00:46:58.380 --> 00:47:00.690
then you're going to have crappy science.

00:47:00.690 --> 00:47:02.610
So I believe in people,
and I believe in science.

00:47:02.610 --> 00:47:04.105
And together that's

00:47:04.105 --> 00:47:05.871
what the Lab Jumpstart program represents.

00:47:05.871 --> 00:47:07.863
So I hope you'll consider it.

00:47:08.967 --> 00:47:11.150
We love our students.

00:47:11.150 --> 00:47:13.010
We keep in touch with our students...

00:47:13.010 --> 00:47:14.500
And exactly.

00:47:14.500 --> 00:47:15.333
Oda wrote,

00:47:15.333 --> 00:47:18.310
we want you to be
successful in whatever path,

00:47:18.310 --> 00:47:20.550
and just have an appreciation for science.

00:47:20.550 --> 00:47:22.770
You don't have to like be a scientist.

00:47:22.770 --> 00:47:25.290
We just know how it works.

00:47:25.290 --> 00:47:28.180
I mean how amazing is it
to have scientific literacy

00:47:28.180 --> 00:47:30.240
in an age that we're in right now,

00:47:30.240 --> 00:47:31.500
when we're going through.

00:47:31.500 --> 00:47:34.253
Moderna just came out with like a vaccine,

00:47:35.540 --> 00:47:36.810
efficacy studies.

00:47:36.810 --> 00:47:39.550
Pfizer came out with
vaccine efficacy studies.

00:47:39.550 --> 00:47:43.200
You want to be able to navigate
this type of information.

00:47:43.200 --> 00:47:45.600
That's so impactful for our lives.

00:47:45.600 --> 00:47:46.433
That's our goal.

00:47:46.433 --> 00:47:48.435
We just want you to be
cool with that stuff.

00:47:48.435 --> 00:47:50.495
You can go and do whatever you want.

00:47:50.495 --> 00:47:51.940
- [Odaelys] (indistinct)
interest in science.

00:47:51.940 --> 00:47:54.495
So we're looking for students who,

00:47:54.495 --> 00:47:58.840
after this presentation or
some class that you've taken,

00:47:58.840 --> 00:48:01.560
you became super interested in
finding out a little bit more

00:48:01.560 --> 00:48:03.370
or wanting to do something more hands-on

00:48:03.370 --> 00:48:05.250
in terms of getting to know...

00:48:05.250 --> 00:48:06.897
Y'all are getting a feel

00:48:06.897 --> 00:48:08.497
for what science is really like.

00:48:09.620 --> 00:48:11.489
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:48:11.489 --> 00:48:14.283
I'll put out that
information to them again.

00:48:15.416 --> 00:48:17.340
And I have to let them go
in a couple of minutes.

00:48:17.340 --> 00:48:19.420
They have a fourth period class,

00:48:19.420 --> 00:48:21.160
but we really appreciate you all.

00:48:21.160 --> 00:48:22.630
And we love y'all.

00:48:22.630 --> 00:48:23.690
We love science,

00:48:23.690 --> 00:48:28.690
and we wish you all a wonderful
rest of the fall and winter.

00:48:29.180 --> 00:48:30.630
We'll stay in touch for sure.

00:48:32.450 --> 00:48:33.760
- Thanks everyone.

00:48:33.760 --> 00:48:35.512
- Have a great day.

00:48:35.512 --> 00:48:38.595
- [Teacher] Thank you, Miss Eckartt.

